# 40. FINAL DEFINITION OF SUCCESS

The application is successful when I can repeatedly:

* Answer questions correctly
* Explain why the answer is correct
* Distinguish similar AWS concepts
* Handle mixed topics
* Handle scenario questions
* Retain previously learned concepts
* Perform consistently under timed conditions
* Identify and eliminate my recurring mistakes

Do not declare me ready simply because I finished the question bank.

The system should continuously expose weaknesses until my performance becomes consistently strong.

